    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3692db12_c8bca3a3",
        "filename": "common/smbus.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 34,
      "author": {
        "id": 1103909
      },
      "writtenOn": "2014-08-01T20:55:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is just really confusing. The smbus_wr_if has a data array of size 0, but yet you are accessing element n-1. It only works because you have typecast some other struct with more data elements as a smbus_wr_if struct.\n\nI think we should only have one struct, and it should be private to this file. It should have slave_addr, smbus_cmd, data_size, and pointer to data buffer. We can use that for reads and writes of any size. We can build the CRC incrementally instead of all at once.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 34,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 34,
        "endChar": 12
      },
      "revId": "a35f79c70778e65036231a0dc86c0185b03533ac",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
